            <ArticleTitle>[Evaluation of the safety and clinical feasibility of exercise 99mTc-MIBI SPECT using one day protocol--multicenter phase III clinical trial report].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>929-38</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We evaluated the safety and clinical usefulness of the same day protocol of exercise 99mTc-MIBI SPECT in 107 patients with heart diseases. No adverse event was observed except for one case of transient hypotension caused by the exercise. More than 95% of stress images and all of the rest images were judged as &quot;Excellent&quot; or &quot;Good&quot; in image quality. Overall sensitivity was 84.3% in detecting coronary artery disease, and no statistical difference was observed between the results obtained with Re-Ex and Ex-Re protocols. The examination was &quot;Quite Effective&quot; or &quot;Effective&quot; in diagnostic efficacy in 96.2% of the cases. We concluded that the same day protocol is a safe and useful method for diagnosing myocardial ischemia, which provides high image quality and valuable information.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
